The lab-process-mail tool bases work on trunk. That makes sense for a
general contributor, but lab-claude is my personal coding assistant. I
would run it inline in my shell if I trusted it, but I don't.

That means that it should behave differently than an ordinary
contributor. While a typical contributor would want to base work on
trunk, my coding assistant should see pretty much the same view I
do. b/dev is the branch I use to stage and test work before
committing. In effect, all the commits in b/dev are potential targets
for the next trunk move.

lab-claude will be much more effective if it bases work on b/dev.

In fact, I think this should be configurable. It should default to
'trunk()' the jj revset. But it should be configurable via env var
`LAB_BASE_BRANCH` so I would run with
e.g. `LAB_BASE_BRANCH=b/dev@upstream lab-process-mail`
